{"id":32588,"date":"2025-08-07T17:34:07","date_gmt":"2025-08-07T21:34:07","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/?page_id=32588"},"modified":"2025-10-14T13:19:32","modified_gmt":"2025-10-14T17:19:32","slug":"apd-therapy-and-management","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/apd-therapy-and-management\/","title":{"rendered":"APD Therapy and Management"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile is-vertically-aligned-center auditory-processing-image-1\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"516\" height=\"625\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/09\/auditoryprocessingdisorderguidebyelevateaudiologydocument1.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32644 size-full\"\/><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\">Elevate Audiology\u2019s<br>\u201cAuditory Processing Disorder Guide\u201d<\/h2>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p>Are you interested in learning more about APD? Request a complimentary copy of our Auditory Processing Disorder Guide by Dr. Katelyn Ooms by filling out the form below.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<iframe\n\n    src=\" https:\/\/system.elevateaudiology.com\/widget\/form\/RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    style=\"width:100%;height:100%;border:none;border-radius:3px\"\n\n    id=\"inline-RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    data-layout=\"{'id':'INLINE'}\"\n\n    data-trigger-type=\"alwaysShow\"\n\n    data-trigger-value=\"\"\n\n    data-activation-type=\"alwaysActivated\"\n\n    data-activation-value=\"\"\n\n    data-deactivation-type=\"neverDeactivate\"\n\n    data-deactivation-value=\"\"\n\n    data-form-name=\"APD Report Opt In Form\"\n\n    data-height=\"884\"\n\n    data-layout-iframe-id=\"inline-RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    data-form-id=\"RKvRDMWuUNpjx11JEY6i\"\n\n    title=\"APD Report Opt In Form\"\n\n>\n\n<\/iframe>\n\n<script src=\" https:\/\/system.elevateaudiology.com\/js\/form_embed.js%22%3e%3c\/script\"><\/script>\n\n\n\n<p>Managing Auditory Processing Disorder (APD) requires a structured, individualized approach that targets both the underlying auditory deficits and their real-world impact. At our clinic, we follow a three-pronged management model based on the work of Dr. Ferre and Dr. Bellis, which includes&nbsp;environmental modifications,&nbsp;direct therapy and&nbsp;compensatory strategies. This holistic framework allows us to address the core processing challenges while also supporting functional success at home, school and in the workplace.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"988\" height=\"556\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy11.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32591\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy11.avif 988w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy11-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy11-600x338.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 988px) 100vw, 988px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"988\" height=\"556\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy21.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32592\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy21.avif 988w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy21-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy21-600x338.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 988px) 100vw, 988px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"988\" height=\"556\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy31.avif\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-32593\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy31.avif 988w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy31-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/08\/apdtherapy31-600x338.jpg 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 988px) 100vw, 988px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">1. Environmental Modifications<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>&nbsp;We work closely with families, educators and clients to recommend listening environments that support auditory success. This includes strategies such as preferential classroom seating, reducing background noise, using visual supports and, in some cases, recommending assistive listening devices like personal FM or remote microphone systems. These modifications help reduce the listener&#8217;s cognitive load and improve access to auditory information.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">2. Direct Auditory Therapy<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>&nbsp;Our clinic provides both&nbsp;individualized one-on-one therapy sessions and&nbsp;home-based digital therapy programs. One-on-one therapy is based on the&nbsp;Buffalo Model of Auditory Therapy. For those seeking flexibility, we also offer access to guided online therapy programs that can be completed at home to reinforce and generalize skills. These evidence-based exercises help strengthen different aspects of auditory processing that an individual may be struggling with.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">3. Compensatory Strategies<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>&nbsp;In addition to therapy, we recommend practical strategies to compensate for auditory weaknesses. This may include active listening techniques, improving self-advocacy skills, note-taking methods or rehearsal strategies to support working memory. These tools empower individuals to independently manage their challenges in academic, professional and social settings.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Our goal is to equip each client with the tools and support needed to improve listening skills, boost confidence and succeed across communication settings. Therapy plans are personalized, and progress is regularly monitored to ensure meaningful outcomes.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Here\u2019s a link to our FAQ page, where you can find clear answers to common questions about our APD program and what to expect: <a href=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/auditory-processing-disorder-apd-faq\/\">Click here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Call Elevate Audiology at <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-6611\">(864) 447-6611<\/a> for the Easley office or <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-4183\">(864) 447-4183<\/a> for the Greenville office for more information or to schedule an appointment.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Elevate Audiology\u2019s\u201cAuditory Processing Disorder Guide\u201d Are you interested in learning more about APD? Request a complimentary copy of our Auditory Processing Disorder Guide by Dr. Katelyn Ooms by filling out the form below. Managing Auditory Processing Disorder (APD) requires a structured, individualized approach that targets both the underlying auditory deficits and their real-world impact. At&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":3,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"","_seopress_titles_desc":"","_seopress_robots_index":"","schema":"","fname":"","lname":"","position":"","credentials":"","placeID":"","no_match":false,"name":"","company":"","review":"","address":"","city":"","state":"","zip":"","lat":"","lng":"","phone1":"","